        "species": "Diplocaulus natatorinutrix",
        "time": "Permian",
        "diet": "Piscivore",
        "temperament": "Skittish",
        "wild": "Diplocaulus natatorinutrix is a small, skittish amphibian that flees at the first sign of trouble. Its most striking feature is its boomerang-shaped head, which houses large chambers that store a remarkable volume of oxygen. It lives along riverbanks and in swamps, diving beneath the water when threatened.",
        "domesticated": "The Diplocaulus's head chambers allow it to store and provide oxygen to nearby creatures and riders. When a survivor holds onto a tamed Diplocaulus while swimming, they can breathe from its oxygen reserve, enabling extended underwater exploration without needing a SCUBA tank or high oxygen stats. It functions as a living rebreather for its owner."
